n of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-2,-2),$ we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-2)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 4 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "632cbcfb9d0fd3ec982dc5ba03e81722280c96e8f4b9edd38941b606dac2b975" "basis" 1487 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02c72d6aa9aa414c46a7b45bf109fc01e3bfd03d807393d717271958bcbf57c5" "basis" 1487 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/state.json" "file_sha256" "632cbcfb9d0fd3ec982dc5ba03e81722280c96e8f4b9edd38941b606dac2b975" "basis" 1487 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}y"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cours