abola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(3,2).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(3,2),$ we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {2}^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 4 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{1}{3}$ is positive." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b88b47ffba4f1cca609405a7a46f39d9237523db60eb50068f0e025412a3aa0"} {"question" "q-115601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{9}{2}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{9}{8}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-