ory" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b88b47ffba4f1cca609405a7a46f39d9237523db60eb50068f0e025412a3aa0"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=2y"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-2x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=4x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-2x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at  $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(8,4),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 16 & =32p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b88b47ffba4f1cca609405a7a46f39d9237523db60eb50068f0e025412a3aa0"} {"question" "q-11753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=-2x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-4x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=2x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=4x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=6x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=2x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-8,8).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-8,8),$ we can substitute $x=-8$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\ 64 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-2)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b88b47ffba4f1cca609405a7a46f39d9237523db60eb50068f0e025412a3aa0"} {"question" "q-11751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=-4x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-6x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-8x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=6x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=8x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-8x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at  $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(6,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(6,3),$ we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=3$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {3}^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\ 9 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{8})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b88b47ffba4f1cca609405a7a46f39d9237523db60eb50068f0e025412a3aa0"} {"question" "q-115628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}=12y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}y"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=3x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{8}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/8a48fcacc437d1dca41df82e24984507a92d686f80f4517c6682e8b14b694f0e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(-6,0)$ and passes through the point $(-2,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-6,0),$ we substitute $h=-6$ and $k=0$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-2,6),$ so we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=6$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+6) \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(-2+6) \\\\ 36 & =16p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+6) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{4})(x+6) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9(x+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{9}{4}$ is positive." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b88b47ffba4f1cca609405a7a46f39d9237523db60eb50068f0e025412a3aa0"} {"question" "q-11809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y+6)^{2}=9x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-6(x+6)"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-9(x+6)"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=6(x+6)"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=9(x+6)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=9(x+6)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/872c4385f2f7075ac4f9690f5adabaa8cb6b4ad3ffe738b47f2b22e477aab621.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(4,-4)$ and passes through the point $(0,-6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(4,-4),$ we substitute $h=4$ and $k=-4$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+4)^{2} & =4p(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(0,-6),$ so we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=-6$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+4)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (-6+4)^{2} & =4p(0-4) \\\\ 4 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+4)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{4})(x-4) \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =-(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is negative." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b88b47ffba4f1cca609405a7a46f39d9237523db60eb50068f0e025412a3aa0"} {"question" "q-11799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-11799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y+4)^{2}=(x-4)"] ["math" "(y+4)^{2}=-(x-4)"] ["math" "(y+4)^{2}=-2(x-4)"] ["math" "(y+4)^{2}=2(x-4)"] ["math" "(y-4)^{2}=-(x+4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha25