s of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(3,3)$ and passes through the point $(6,-3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(3,3),$ we substitute $h=3$ and $k=3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(6,-3),$ so we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3) \\\\ (-3-3)^{2} & =4p(6-3) \\\\ 36 & =12p \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3) \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =4(3)(x-3) \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =12(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=3$ is positive." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b88b47ffba4f1cca609405a7a46f39d9237523db60eb50068f0e025412a3aa0"} {"question" "q-115640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/state.json" "file_sha256" "610aa6b2bb4ffb9544fff25cbc0cb9921548e03c007431fe4f7a0356ca138ec9"} {"question" "q-115640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["mat